NullWire is an independent Telegram API desktop client built from Telegram Desktop sources.
This package is an isolated source-build test and uses the limited sample API identity.
It is not suitable for login, migration or publication to the stable APT repository.

Complete source inputs, bundled dependency sources, the build-toolchain archives and
Debian recipes are provided by the source package in OBS:
https://build.opensuse.org/package/show/home:dwolfF:telegram:staging/nullwire-buildtest

Packaging and patches:
https://github.com/lmdeuser/nullwire-ubuntu-obs

Upstream:
https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop/releases/tag/v7.4.1

Native hardware video decoding defaults to enabled on Linux. The upstream backend
selector and software fallback are preserved. Hardware and driver support varies.
Existing user preferences are not overwritten by the new default.
